{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"55069","self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/55069","key":"SV-8935","renderedFields":{"statuscategorychangedate":"Today 10:27 AM","issuetype":null,"timespent":null,"project":null,"customfield_10351":"","fixVersions":null,"aggregatetimespent":null,"statusCategory":null,"resolution":null,"resolutiondate":null,"workratio":null,"watches":null,"issuerestriction":null,"lastViewed":null,"created":"Today 10:27 AM","customfield_10021":null,"customfield_10385":null,"priority":null,"labels":null,"customfield_10016":null,"customfield_10019":null,"timeestimate":null,"aggregatetimeoriginalestimate":null,"versions":null,"customfield_10418":null,"customfield_10419":null,"issuelinks":null,"assignee":null,"updated":"Today 10:27 AM","status":null,"components":null,"timeoriginalestimate":null,"description":"<h3><a name=\"1.Whathappensnow\"></a>1. What happens now</h3>\n\n<p>The Parts Velocity spreadsheet download prints the \"Last Sale\" column as a piece of text such as <tt>54 days</tt> instead of the plain number <tt>54</tt>.</p>\n\n<p>Because the cell is text and not a number, somebody who opens the file in Excel cannot sort by it or use it in a calculation without cleaning the column first.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"2.Whatshouldhappeninstead\"></a>2. What should happen instead</h3>\n\n<p>The written description asks for the wording only in the PDF, and a plain number in the spreadsheet.</p>\n\n<p>Parts Velocity specification, version 5, requirement S6-R8: \"Last Sale renders as N days (e.g. 42 days) in the PDF; the CSV renders the raw integer.\"</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"3.Howtoseeit\"></a>3. How to see it</h3>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Sign in as a user who can see reports and open <b>Reports</b> &gt; <b>Parts Velocity</b>.</li>\n\t<li>In the report's own search box type <b>BRAKECLEAN</b>.</li>\n\t<li>Open the three-dot menu at the top of the report and choose <b>Download (CSV)</b>.</li>\n\t<li>Open the downloaded file and look at the <b>Last Sale</b> column.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<p><b>Exact test data this was seen with:</b> part number <b>BRAKECLEAN</b>, description <b>Brake &amp; Parts Cleaner</b>, locations <b>Staging Heavy Duty - 9919</b> and <b>Staging Lethbridge - 4310</b>, date range <b>This Year</b>. The file is named <b>velocity-report.csv</b>.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"4.Whatwasactuallyinthefile\"></a>4. What was actually in the file</h3>\n\n{noquote}<br/>\nInventory,BRAKECLEAN,\"Brake &amp; Parts Cleaner\",HD-Fluids,—,\"Staging Heavy Duty - 9919\",512.00,$4.79,$7.69,\"$4,332.11\",\"$1,634.06\",37.7%,416,\"54 days\",618.00{noquote}\n\n<p>The cell reads <tt>\"54 days\"</tt> where it should read <tt>54</tt>.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"5.Whatwasruledout\"></a>5. What was ruled out</h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><b>It is not the PDF.</b> The PDF correctly prints <b>54 days</b>, which is what the written description asks the PDF to do. Only the spreadsheet is wrong.</li>\n\t<li><b>It is not one part.</b> Every row in the file carries the same wording.</li>\n\t<li><b>It is not an empty value.</b> A part with no sale at all correctly prints an em dash in both files, so the empty case is handled properly.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<h3><a name=\"6.Howoften\"></a>6. How often</h3>\n\n<p>Every time. Four spreadsheet downloads out of four.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"7.Whereitwasseen\"></a>7. Where it was seen</h3>\n\n<p>Reports &gt; Parts Velocity, on the QA branch, build v3.5-16cf83f, on 6 August 2026.</p>","customfield_10015":null,"timetracking":{},"security":null,"aggregatetimeestimate":null,"attachment":[],"summary":null,"creator":null,"subtasks":null,"customfield_10285":"","reporter":null,"customfield_10044":null,"aggregateprogress":null,"customfield_10046":null,"customfield_10047":null,"environment":"","customfield_10318":null,"duedate":null,"customfield_10518":null,"progress":null,"votes":null,"comment":{"comments":[],"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/55069/comment","maxResults":0,"total":0,"startAt":0},"worklog":{"startAt":0,"maxResults":20,"total":0,"worklogs":[]}},"fields":{"statuscategorychangedate":"2026-08-06T00:27:17.802-0500","issuetype":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issuetype/10007","id":"10007","description":"Subtasks track small pieces of work that are part of a larger task. (Migrated on 31 Dec 2023 09:01 UTC)","iconUrl":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10854?size=medium","name":"Story Defect","subtask":true,"avatarId":10854,"entityId":"0900502c-ae66-465f-a9da-8322307b07ff","hierarchyLevel":-1},"parent":{"id":"54667","key":"SV-8646","self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/54667","fields":{"summary":"Velocity - Story 6 - Exports (CSV & PDF)","status":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/status/10349","description":"","iconUrl":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/","name":"Open","id":"10349","statusCategory":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/statuscategory/2","id":2,"key":"new","colorName":"blue-gray","name":"To Do"}},"priority":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/priority/3","iconUrl":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/images/icons/priorities/medium_new.svg","name":"Medium","id":"3"},"issuetype":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issuetype/10245","id":"10245","description":"Stories track functionality or features expressed as user goals.","iconUrl":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10315?size=medium","name":"Story","subtask":false,"avatarId":10315,"entityId":"2d932db9-30a4-451f-aa74-561885726568","hierarchyLevel":0}}},"timespent":null,"project":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/project/10001","id":"10001","key":"SV","name":"ShopView","projectTypeKey":"software","simplified":true,"avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/universal_avatar/view/type/project/avatar/10551","24x24"